sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Main as run_benchmark.main()
    participant Run as BenchmarkRunner
    participant SSH as PiSSH
    participant PMIC as PmicMonitor
    participant Smp as _sampler_loop (thread)
    participant Pi as Raspberry Pi (via SSH)
    participant H as Moduli helper<br/>datasets_loader / integrity /<br/>thermal / llama_parser /<br/>scoring / analysis

    Note over Main,Run: 1) Inizializzazione
    Main->>Main: cfg = load_config(config.json)
    Main->>PMIC: PmicMonitor(pi_cfg, pmic_cfg)
    Main->>SSH: PiSSH(pi_cfg, ready_prompt)
    Main->>Run: BenchmarkRunner(cfg, power=PMIC, ssh=SSH)

    Main->>Run: load_samples()
    Run->>H: datasets_loader.load_all(benchmarks)
    H-->>Run: samples[] (con cap max_samples_per_benchmark)

    Note over Main,Pi: 2) setup_hardware()
    Main->>Run: setup_hardware()
    Run->>PMIC: connect()
    PMIC->>Pi: SSH dedicata + vcgencmd pmic_read_adc (test)
    Run->>PMIC: configure_power() / power_on()
    Run->>SSH: wait_for_boot_and_connect()
    SSH->>Pi: connessione SSH
    Run->>SSH: open_shell()
    SSH->>Pi: invoke_shell() (shell interattiva)
    Run->>H: integrity.verify(ssh, cfg)
    loop per ogni modello (6)
        H->>SSH: run_command("sha256sum <modello>")
        SSH->>Pi: exec sha256sum
        Pi-->>H: hash
    end
    H-->>Run: OK (o RuntimeError se hash cambiato)
    Run->>PMIC: measure_idle_bias()
    PMIC->>Smp: start_recording() -> avvia thread
    Note over Smp,Pi: campiona ~20 s, poi media = P_idle
    PMIC->>Smp: stop_recording()

    Note over Main,H: 3) run() — per modello x thread x ripetizione
    Main->>Run: run()
    loop modello x thread(1/2/4) x ripetizione(3)
        Run->>Run: _run_one(model, threads, rep)
        Run->>Run: build_command(...)
        Run->>H: thermal.read_state(ssh)  [stato base]
        H->>SSH: measure_temp() / get_throttled_raw()
        SSH->>Pi: vcgencmd measure_temp / get_throttled
        Run->>PMIC: new_project() / start_recording()
        PMIC->>Smp: avvia campionamento

        par In background, fino a stop_recording()
            loop a ~10 Hz
                Smp->>PMIC: _read_power()
                PMIC->>Pi: vcgencmd pmic_read_adc
                Pi-->>Smp: I,V dei 12 rami -> append (t, P)
            end
        end

        Run->>PMIC: t_load0 = mark()
        Run->>SSH: launch_model(command, load_timeout)
        SSH->>Pi: avvio llama-cli, attesa prompt ">"
        Run->>PMIC: t_load1 = mark()

        loop per ogni campione (prompt)
            Run->>SSH: clear_history()
            SSH->>Pi: "/clear"
            Run->>SSH: stage_prompt(prompt)
            Run->>PMIC: t0 = mark()
            Run->>SSH: submit_prompt(infer_timeout)
            SSH->>Pi: invia prompt, attende riga timing
            Pi-->>SSH: risposta + "[ Prompt.. | Generation.. ]"
            SSH-->>Run: raw
            Run->>PMIC: t1 = mark()
            Run->>H: thermal.read_state(ssh)  [se log_per_inference]
            Run->>H: llama_parser.extract_response(raw, prompt)
            Run->>H: scoring.score(btype, response, expected)
            H-->>Run: {score, parsed, ...}
        end

        Run->>SSH: stop_model()
        SSH->>Pi: Ctrl-C (esce da llama-cli)
        Run->>H: llama_parser.parse_timings(...)
        Run->>PMIC: rec = stop_recording()
        PMIC->>Smp: ferma il thread
        Smp-->>PMIC: campioni [(t,P), ...]
        Run->>PMIC: window_energy(rec, t_load0, t_load1)  [riga load]
        loop per ogni campione
            Run->>PMIC: window_energy(rec, t0, t1)
            PMIC-->>Run: {energy_net_j, avg_power_w, ...}
            Run->>Run: _mk_row(...)
        end
        Run-->>Run: rows, throttled (retry se throttling, max_retries)
    end

    Note over Main,H: 4) Salvataggio e chiusura
    Main->>Run: save_csv()
    Run->>Run: scrive recordings/results.csv
    Main->>Run: teardown()
    Run->>SSH: stop_model() / close()
    SSH->>Pi: chiude shell e connessione
    Run->>PMIC: power_off() / disconnect()
    PMIC->>Pi: chiude connessione SSH del PMIC

    Note over Main,H: 5) Analisi
    Main->>H: analysis.run_analysis(csv, cfg)
    H->>H: load_results / aggregate / per_config /<br/>total_energy_per_config / composite_score
    H->>H: plot_* -> recordings/plots/*.png
